{"additionalPlain":"Why Join Assist World?\n \n100% REMOTE\n$50 birthday bonus\n$200 testimonial bonus\nNO TRACKER. NO PROBLEM\n","additional":"<div><strong>Why Join Assist World?</strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>100% REMOTE</div>\n<div>$50 birthday&nbsp;bonus</div>\n<div>$200 testimonial bonus</div>\n<div>NO TRACKER. NO PROBLEM</div>","categories":{"commitment":"Executive Assistant / Operations","department":"Sales Operations","location":"South Africa","team":"Revenue Operations","allLocations":["South Africa","Philippines"]},"createdAt":1781907195238,"descriptionPlain":"About Us\nWe’re supporting a venture-backed startup helping some of the world's most innovative\nconsumer technology companies optimize their products through AI-driven experimentation.\n\nThey design and deploy experiments that improve user experience, increase engagement, and\ndrive revenue growth.\n\nThey're a small, ambitious team of five people who move quickly, value craftsmanship, and care\ndeeply about building exceptional products. We believe in high ownership, high standards, and\nusing technology to amplify human capability.\n\nThe Role\n\nWe're looking for an exceptionally capable Executive Assistant / Operations Associate to\nbecome a force multiplier for our founder.\nThis isn't a traditional EA role.\n\nOne day you might be coordinating international travel and researching the best neighborhood\nto stay in for a customer visit. The next, you could be sourcing catering for a private industry\nevent, preparing customer documents, managing outreach campaigns, or helping streamline\ninternal operations.\n\nYou'll work across both professional and personal logistics, helping eliminate operational\nbottlenecks so leadership can stay focused on building the company.\n\nIf you're someone who thrives on solving problems, figuring things out independently, and\nleveraging AI tools to move faster than everyone else, you'll love this role.\n","description":"<div><strong>About Us<br></strong><br>We’re supporting a venture-backed startup helping some of the world's most innovative<br>consumer technology companies optimize their products through AI-driven experimentation.<br><br>They design and deploy experiments that improve user experience, increase engagement, and<br>drive revenue growth.<br><br>They're a small, ambitious team of five people who move quickly, value craftsmanship, and care<br>deeply about building exceptional products. We believe in high ownership, high standards, and<br>using technology to amplify human capability.<br><br><strong>The Role</strong><br><br>We're looking for an exceptionally capable Executive Assistant / Operations Associate to<br>become a force multiplier for our founder.<br>This isn't a traditional EA role.<br><br>One day you might be coordinating international travel and researching the best neighborhood<br>to stay in for a customer visit. The next, you could be sourcing catering for a private industry<br>event, preparing customer documents, managing outreach campaigns, or helping streamline<br>internal operations.<br><br>You'll work across both professional and personal logistics, helping eliminate operational<br>bottlenecks so leadership can stay focused on building the company.<br><br>If you're someone who thrives on solving problems, figuring things out independently, and<br>leveraging AI tools to move faster than everyone else, you'll love this role.</div>","id":"7f103914-0e71-4f58-941a-a806ff9b474b","lists":[{"text":"What You'll Be Doing","content":"<div><strong>Executive Support</strong><br>● Manage complex international travel, flights, accommodation, and logistics<br>● Research optimal locations for business trips based on customer meetings and<br>schedules<br>● Coordinate calendars, appointments, and meetings<br>● Handle administrative tasks and founder support requests<br><br><strong>Operations</strong><br>● Research vendors, suppliers, and service providers<br>● Source and negotiate with meal prep providers, event vendors, and operational partners<br>● Coordinate company events, dinners, and networking activities<br>● Create, edit, and manage business documents using existing templates<br>● Support internal operational projects and process improvements<br><br><strong>Sales &amp; Outreach Support</strong><br>● Assist with LinkedIn outreach and account-based prospecting<br>● Conduct company and market research<br>● Help maintain prospect and customer information<br>● Support event attendee coordination and follow-up<br><br><strong>Research &amp; Problem Solving</strong><br>● Compare options and provide recommendations across a wide variety of business and<br>personal tasks<br>● Conduct deep research and present concise findings<br>● Solve ambiguous operational challenges with minimal direction<br>● Proactively identify improvements and opportunities</div>"},{"text":"What We're Looking For","content":"<div><strong>Essential</strong><br>● 5+ years of experience as an Executive Assistant, Operations Coordinator, Chief of<br>Staff, or similar role<br>● Exceptional written English communication skills<br>● Strong research and analytical abilities<br>● Highly organized with excellent attention to detail<br>● Proven ability to work independently with minimal supervision<br>● Comfortable managing multiple priorities simultaneously<br>● Strong judgment and problem-solving skills<br><br><strong>AI-Native Mindset (Required)</strong><br>You must be an enthusiastic user of modern AI tools.<br>We're looking for someone who already uses tools such as:<br>● Claude<br>● ChatGPT<br>● Codex<br>● Cursor<br>● AI agents and workflow automation tools<br><br>You do not need to be a software engineer, but you must be comfortable working alongside AI<br>systems and using them daily to increase productivity.<br><br><strong>Personal Attributes</strong><br>● High agency: you take ownership and figure things out<br>● Curious and resourceful<br>● Fast learner<br>● Strong commercial awareness<br>● Comfortable operating in ambiguity<br>● Motivated by excellence and craftsmanship<br>● Excited by startups, technology, and AI</div>"},{"text":"Nice to Have","content":"<div>● Startup experience<br>● Experience supporting founders or executives<br>● Event coordination experience<br>● Sales development or outbound outreach experience<br>● Familiarity with GitHub-based knowledge management<br>● Experience working with distributed teams</div>"}],"salaryRange":{"min":1000,"max":1400,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-month-salary"},"salaryDescription":"<div><strong>Location</strong>: Remote<br><strong>Type</strong>: Full-Time (40 hours per week)</div>","salaryDescriptionPlain":"Location: Remote\nType: Full-Time (40 hours per week)\n","text":"EA / Operations Assistant (AI-Native)","country":"ZA","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div><strong>About Us<br></strong><br>We&rsquo;re supporting a venture-backed startup helping some of the world's most innovative<br>consumer technology companies optimize their products through AI-driven experimentation.<br><br>They design and deploy experiments that improve user experience, increase engagement, and<br>drive revenue growth.<br><br>They're a small, ambitious team of five people who move quickly, value craftsmanship, and care<br>deeply about building exceptional products. We believe in high ownership, high standards, and<br>using technology to amplify human capability.<br><br><strong>The Role</strong><br><br>We're looking for an exceptionally capable Executive Assistant / Operations Associate to<br>become a force multiplier for our founder.<br>This isn't a traditional EA role.<br><br>One day you might be coordinating international travel and researching the best neighborhood<br>to stay in for a customer visit. The next, you could be sourcing catering for a private industry<br>event, preparing customer documents, managing outreach campaigns, or helping streamline<br>internal operations.<br><br>You'll work across both professional and personal logistics, helping eliminate operational<br>bottlenecks so leadership can stay focused on building the company.<br><br>If you're someone who thrives on solving problems, figuring things out independently, and<br>leveraging AI tools to move faster than everyone else, you'll love this role.</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"About Us\nWe’re supporting a venture-backed startup helping some of the world's most innovative\nconsumer technology companies optimize their products through AI-driven experimentation.\n\nThey design and deploy experiments that improve user experience, increase engagement, and\ndrive revenue growth.\n\nThey're a small, ambitious team of five people who move quickly, value craftsmanship, and care\ndeeply about building exceptional products. We believe in high ownership, high standards, and\nusing technology to amplify human capability.\n\nThe Role\n\nWe're looking for an exceptionally capable Executive Assistant / Operations Associate to\nbecome a force multiplier for our founder.\nThis isn't a traditional EA role.\n\nOne day you might be coordinating international travel and researching the best neighborhood\nto stay in for a customer visit. The next, you could be sourcing catering for a private industry\nevent, preparing customer documents, managing outreach campaigns, or helping streamline\ninternal operations.\n\nYou'll work across both professional and personal logistics, helping eliminate operational\nbottlenecks so leadership can stay focused on building the company.\n\nIf you're someone who thrives on solving problems, figuring things out independently, and\nleveraging AI tools to move faster than everyone else, you'll love this role.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/assist-world/7f103914-0e71-4f58-941a-a806ff9b474b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/assist-world/7f103914-0e71-4f58-941a-a806ff9b474b/apply"}